    "body": "> **Draft for legal review. Not in force. Not legal advice.**\n\nThese terms are between **Awning** (ABN to be inserted) and the business that subscribes\nto it — called \"you\" below. They cover the website builder, the hosting of the website\nit produces, and anything else we provide with it.\n\nWe have tried to write them in plain English. Where a term sounds one-sided, it usually\nis not allowed to be: you are a small business, and standard-form contracts with small\nbusinesses are subject to the unfair contract terms rules in the Australian Consumer\nLaw. If something here reads as unfair to you, tell us — we would rather fix the term\nthan argue about it.\n\n## 1. What we provide\n\nWe provide a service that builds a website for your business from what you tell us\nabout it, lets you edit that website, and publishes it on the internet at a subdomain we\nprovide or a domain you own.\n\nWe do not provide legal, tax, marketing or business advice, and nothing the AI writes is\nany of those things.\n\n## 2. What you are responsible for\n\nThe content of your website is yours. You are responsible for it being true.\n\nThat matters more than it sounds. The AI writes a first draft from what you tell it, and\nit is quite capable of writing a confident sentence about your business that is not\naccurate. **Read your site before you publish it.** Claims about your business —\nqualifications, licences, years of experience, awards, prices, guarantees, what you can\ndo and how fast — are representations you are making to your customers, and the\nAustralian Consumer Law holds you to them, not us.\n\nWe build guardrails against the obvious failures: the system will not invent\ntestimonials, will not fabricate credentials or awards, and will not write a countdown\nto a deadline that does not exist. Those guardrails reduce the risk. They do not\ntransfer it.\n\nYou are also responsible for:\n\n- having the right to use any image, logo or text you upload\n- your own licence and registration obligations for the trade you are in\n- the personal information your website collects from your customers, and for having a\n  privacy policy that describes it (we generate one, but it is yours)\n- keeping your account credentials to yourself\n\n## 3. Acceptable use\n\nOur [Acceptable Use Policy](./ACCEPTABLE-USE.md) forms part of these terms. It is short\nand it is mostly obvious.\n\n## 4. Fees, GST and price changes\n\nPrices are shown in Australian dollars and **include GST**.\n\nSubscriptions are billed monthly or annually in advance and renew automatically until\nyou cancel. We will email you before each annual renewal.\n\nIf we change the price, we will give you at least **30 days' notice by email** before it\ntakes effect, and you may cancel before then without penalty. A price change never\napplies to a period you have already paid for. If you do not want the new price, cancel\n— we would rather that than have you feel trapped.\n\nWhere we offer a fixed price for an initial term, that price is fixed for that term.\n\n## 5. Cancelling, and getting your website back\n\nYou can cancel at any time, from your account, without ringing anyone and without\nexplaining yourself.\n\nWhen you cancel, your subscription runs to the end of the period you have paid for and\nthen stops. We do not refund the unused part of a period you chose to end early, except\nwhere the Australian Consumer Law requires it — and if we have got something badly\nwrong, it does.\n\n**Your content is yours and you can take it with you.** On request within 90 days of\ncancelling, we will give you an export of your site's text and images, and we will help\nyou point your own domain somewhere else. We do not hold your domain, your content or\nyour customer enquiries hostage to keep you subscribed.\n\nAfter 90 days we delete your site and its content. Say so before then if you want it\nkept.\n\n## 6. Your customers' personal information\n\nYour website collects personal information from your customers — names, phone numbers,\nemail addresses, whatever they type into an enquiry form. **That information is yours,\nnot ours.** We hold it on your behalf and we only use it to run the service for you.\n\nWe do not sell it. We do not use it for our own marketing. We do not use your customers'\npersonal information to train AI models.\n\nIf there is a data breach affecting it, we will tell you promptly and work with you on\nwhat the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme requires.\n\n## 7. Availability\n\nWe aim to keep your website up. We do not promise it will never be down, and we do not\noffer a service credit scheme at this price — if that is something your business needs,\nwe are probably not the right fit and we would rather tell you now.\n\nWe will give you notice of planned maintenance where we reasonably can.\n\n## 8. Our liability\n\nNothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any guarantee, right or remedy\nyou have under the Australian Consumer Law that cannot lawfully be excluded. If you are\na consumer under that law, you have guarantees that we cannot contract out of, including\nthat our services will be provided with due care and skill and be fit for purpose.\n\nWhere the law allows us to limit our liability, our liability for any claim connected\nwith the service is limited to resupplying the service or paying the cost of having it\nresupplied, at our option.\n\nWe are not liable for loss that we could not reasonably have foreseen, or for loss\ncaused by your own content — including a claim brought against you because of something\nyour website says.\n\n## 9. Suspension and termination\n\nWe may suspend or remove a site that breaches the Acceptable Use Policy. Where it is\nsafe and lawful to do so we will tell you first and give you a chance to fix it. Where\nthe content is seriously harmful or unlawful, we may act immediately and tell you\nstraight after.\n\nWe may suspend a site for non-payment after the grace period described in your billing\nemails. Paying restores it.\n\nIf we terminate your account other than for breach, we refund the unused part of your\ncurrent period.\n\n## 10. Changing these terms\n\nWe may change these terms. For a material change we will give you at least 30 days'\nnotice by email and ask you to accept the new version. Minor changes — fixing a typo,\nclarifying wording that does not change what either of us must do — we may make without\nnotice.\n\nIf you do not accept a material change, you can cancel before it takes effect and we\nwill refund the unused part of your period.\n\n## 11. Disputes and governing law\n\nThese terms are governed by the law of South Australia.\n\nBefore anyone goes anywhere near a court, talk to us. Most things are a misunderstanding\nand we would rather sort it out. If we cannot, you may also be able to take a complaint\nto your state's small business commissioner or to the ACCC.\n\n## 12. Contact\n\nAwning — ABN to be inserted\nEmail to be inserted\nPostal address to be inserted",
